# Copy to `.env` (in mobile/) and fill in. Restart Metro with `npx expo start -c` after any change —
# without `-c` you get the previously baked values and it looks like nothing happened.
#
# Everything here is EXPO_PUBLIC_* — it ships in the app bundle, so ONLY put public/rate-limited
# values here (never a private key or seed phrase).
#
# See CONFIG.md for the full explanation. src/config/env.json is the authoritative list; this file
# is the copy you edit.

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  REQUIRED — a build handed to a member is broken without these four
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Solana mainnet RPC. The public default is rate-limited enough that sends TIME OUT — worst on the
# thing this app does most, an XGO / Token-2022 transfer that also creates the recipient's token
# account. Point this at your backend's RPC proxy so one operator-provided RPC serves every user and
# the key stays server-side:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc
# (or a direct Helius URL — but that embeds the key in the app bundle).
EXPO_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC=

# The platform API — sign-in and the Vault, which share a host. INCLUDE THE PREFIX, and note it is
# /_api, NOT /api: Replit's edge intercepts the literal /api/ prefix and 502s it.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_VAULT_API=https://your-host/_api
# Blank is a working no-op: no sign-in, the Vault opens public links only, and everything falls back
# to the chain and the on-device cache.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VAULT_API=

# The domain the platform is allowed to name in a sign-in challenge. The wallet refuses to sign any
# message that doesn't contain it, so this must match the server's AUTH_DOMAIN *exactly* — a mismatch
# fails on the phone, before the server ever hears about it, and looks like sign-in silently doing
# nothing.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VAULT_DOMAIN=

# The Goshen web app — the SITE, not the API. Site root with no API prefix, e.g. https://goshen.example
# — NOT the /_api value above, even when the two share a host. https only: the app refuses anything
# else rather than handing it to a browser that has the wallet bridged into it.
# Blank leaves More → Marketplace and → Issue a Key visibly disabled.
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEBAPP_URL=

# NOTE ON NETWORKS: the challenge names the cluster and the server refuses one it doesn't speak for.
# This app defaults to mainnet-beta; the platform server defaults to devnet. A deployment that leaves
# the server's SOLANA_CLUSTER unset therefore refuses every real sign-in with a cluster mismatch.

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  OVERRIDE ONLY — a working value is already compiled in
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# dApp connect (WalletConnect) — what lets you scan a desktop screen and sign on your phone.
#
# LEAVE THIS ALONE. A project id is compiled into src/walletconnect/config.ts, so the feature works
# with no configuration. Set this only to point a fork or a second deployment at a different id, or
# to rotate. A blank value here falls back to the built-in id rather than switching the feature off.
#
# Whatever id is active, the Goshen web app must use the SAME one. A mismatch pairs and then silently
# fails to relay, which looks like the wallet ignoring the site.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  OPTIONAL — unset is a legitimate build
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ---- Networks ----
# Solana devnet. The public devnet endpoint is fine for testing.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEVNET_RPC=
# EVM RPCs — public defaults work; set your own (Alchemy/Infura/QuickNode) for real use.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ETH_RPC=
EXPO_PUBLIC_BSC_RPC=
# Prefer routing every network through the backend /api/rpc proxy (keys stay server-side, one shared
# RPC for all users, and it relaxes the client's rate throttle so loads are fast):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_DEVNET_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc?chain=solana-devnet
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_ETH_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc?chain=ethereum
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_BSC_RPC=https://<your-app-host>/api/rpc?chain=bsc

# ---- Features ----
# EVM transaction history (Home + Activity). Free key at etherscan.io/apis (one key, all EVM chains).
# Without it, EVM history is simply hidden.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ETHERSCAN_KEY=
# Push notifications while the app is CLOSED. Needs a real build and an EAS projectId, so it cannot
# work under Expo Go no matter what this is set to. In-app receive alerts (while open) work without it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_NOTIFY_API=
# A JSON list of known-bad addresses — { "solana": [...], "evm": [...] } — fetched at startup and
# warned about before a send. Unset means the small built-in list only.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BLOCKLIST_URL=
# 0x liquidity in the swap comparison (alongside keyless KyberSwap). Prefer the proxy — the key stays
# server-side. The embedded key is a fallback.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ZEROX_PROXY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_ZEROX_API_KEY=
# How much worse a treasury-pool XGO swap may price before the app routes elsewhere, in bps.
# Default 150 (1.5%).
EXPO_PUBLIC_TREASURY_MAX_WORSE_BPS=

# ---- Treasury / launch overrides (normally blank) ----
# The main Global Goshens communal treasury address, shown on the Treasury screen. Blank = the
# built-in address in src/config/treasury.ts, which is the REAL treasury — so you only set this to
# point a build somewhere else. Independent of any multisig: connecting a Squad never changes what
# the treasury view displays.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOSHENS_TREASURY=
# Squads v4 multisig treasury address (optional pre-set). Usually blank — you create or connect a
# Squad in-app (More → Multisig treasury) and it stores on the device. The multisig is its own
# feature and does NOT change the Global Goshens treasury view above.
EXPO_PUBLIC_MULTISIG=
# Community swap fee (0.44% on non-XGO swaps). SOLANA: the treasury WALLET that owns the fee token
# accounts; the fee is taken in the output token and deposited into that wallet's token account for
# the mint (created on-chain automatically on first use). EVM: the treasury's 0x address (blank
# disables EVM fees entirely).
#
# Leave the Solana one BLANK unless you specifically want fees going somewhere other than the
# treasury above — it follows that address rather than repeating it, so the Treasury screen can't
# advertise one account while the money lands in another. Setting it makes them differ, deliberately.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_FEE_OWNER=
EXPO_PUBLIC_EVM_FEE_RECIPIENT=

# ---- Only if sign-in ever moves off the Vault's host ----
# Each falls back to the two required VAULT_* values above, which is why they are normally absent.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_API=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_DOMAIN=
